Adapted source notice: approximate tensor-API dense attention research kernel

src/mlx2/adapters/tensor_fa_research.py contains a Metal kernel body
(TENSOR_FA_SOURCE) adapted from ggml's tensor-API flash attention kernel:

  repository: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
  pull request: 29570 (open, unmerged when read on 2026-10-01)
  revision: 7f0d4d5e0ae391e4ff75512402cb5dd141507244
  file: ggml/src/ggml-metal/kernels/fa_f16.metal (blob 2dfd3799d137fc32bd370e8e637163d8894125e7)
  function: kernel_flash_attn_ext_tensor

Adapted parts: the Q/C/NSG tiling, the tensor_ops matmul2d QK^T and P*V
descriptors, half-rounded scaled queries, half probabilities with the fp32
row sum taken over the same rounded values, the lazy running-max rescale
(only on growth > 8) with a per-row scale and a threadgroup "last rescale"
flag, and the clipped cooperative-tensor store. mlx2 modifications: MLX
mx.fast.metal_kernel wrapping, B1 [1, H, L, D] contiguous layout, in-kernel
causal masking from an explicit absolute query start (finite -FLT_MAX), a
causal KV loop bound, fp32 output, and a race-free atomic threadgroup
engagement counter. Masks, sinks, ALiBi and softcap paths were removed.
Independent review additionally replaced the upstream shared last-rescale
flag with one single-writer flag per SIMD group, reduced after a barrier.

